{
  "title": "Body and health",
  "note": "To say something hurts, use wehtun with the body part as subject: Mein Kopf tut weh; Meine Füße tun weh. German often uses the dative instead of a possessive for your own body: Ich wasche mir die Hände (I wash my hands). Wie geht es dir? asks how someone is.",
  "src": { "t": "Deutsch im Blick, Kapitel 7: Der menschliche Körper", "u": "https://coerll.utexas.edu/dib/voc.php?k=7&s=4" },
